WEBVTT

00:00:00.046 --> 00:00:02.833
The delivery loop starts by establishing the baseline:

00:00:03.274 --> 00:00:06.653
what files, version, and running behavior exist now.

00:00:07.094 --> 00:00:09.044
We then authorize the relevant work.

00:00:09.369 --> 00:00:12.330
Agreement on a design is not automatically permission to

00:00:12.388 --> 00:00:16.416
deploy it, spend money, send messages, or change outside

00:00:16.451 --> 00:00:17.032
systems.

00:00:17.473 --> 00:00:20.503
A kickoff is the concise instruction a new agent can

00:00:20.561 --> 00:00:24.183
follow: where the work lives, which decisions govern it,

00:00:24.427 --> 00:00:27.910
what is allowed, which steps come first, and how to verify

00:00:27.957 --> 00:00:28.595
the result.

00:00:29.036 --> 00:00:32.450
If you already authorized a particular action, the agent

00:00:32.485 --> 00:00:34.981
should honor that authorization rather than ask for it

00:00:35.016 --> 00:00:35.469
again.
